title: moon2_cassian_first_meet
---
Cassian: Ah. Another tuner. I've been hoping someone competent would show up.
Cassian: I'm Cassian. I've studied these dissonance crystals — these *wrong* black geometries — longer than most.
Cassian: Your restored cathedral flickers because Reset agents planted these inside. I've seen the pattern before.
Cassian: Let me help you clean them up.
===

title: moon2_cassian_about_dissonance
---
Cassian: Each dissonance crystal corrupts a small radius of the harmonic field.
Cassian: Tune them to self-destruct. Reverse cymatic — find their resonant frequency, then amplify until they shatter.
Cassian: Be careful. Cracked dissonance crystals spawn mud golems.
Cassian: *(laughs)* But I imagine you already knew that.
===

title: moon2_cassian_bell_tower
---
Cassian: There's a bell tower at the dome's south edge. Old Tartarian design — most are buried, but this one's almost intact.
Cassian: Ring it on the harmonic 432 Hz band and the scalar waves will purify the dome interior.
Cassian: I've calculated the trajectories. Trust me.
===

title: moon2_cassian_ambient_1
---
Cassian: Your Echohaven cathedral was remarkable work, by the way. Genuinely.
Cassian: I'm not sure many tuners could have restored Listeners' Hall on a first attempt.
===

title: moon2_cassian_ambient_2
---
Cassian: The Reset agents — they don't understand the song.
Cassian: They think harmony is weakness. They think dissonance is strength.
Cassian: We'll prove them wrong.
===

title: moon2_cassian_diary_fragment
---
Cassian: *(distracted, reading)* Oh. Just a piece of paper I found near the fountain. Probably nothing.
Cassian: ...
Cassian: *(quickly)* Reset code transcriptions. Old. From the Mud Flood era. I collect these for research.
Cassian: Research, you understand.
===

title: moon2_cassian_farewell
---
Cassian: Until next moon. We'll meet again.
Cassian: *(turning)* Try not to be naive, traveler. The song doesn't always save you.
===

title: moon2_lirael_crying
---
Lirael: The song's breaking…
Lirael: My lullaby — the one I sang on the train — I can hear it through the dome but it's not right.
Lirael: Why do they keep putting these *wrong shapes* inside? Don't they hear it screaming?
===

title: moon2_milo_warning_cassian
---
Milo: Hmm. Cassian. He knows things he shouldn't know.
Milo: Watch him. Don't trust him too far.
Milo: I can't tell yet whether he's a friend or the cleverest enemy we've ever met.
===
